error[ffi_lock_copied]: `b` takes by value a `Box`, whose C struct `struct box` holds a `pthread_mutex_t` at `m`, a copy C forbids
  at tests/golden/unsupported/ffi-lock-copied-a-parameter-taken-by-value.hero:12:15
     |
  12 | function peek(b: Box) -> i64  #~ ffi_lock_copied
     |               ^
  note: a copy of a lock is a second lock holding the first one's state: the copy of a held mutex reads held, and unlocking one leaves the other locked
  note: lend the place instead: a function taking `c: T lent` reads the caller's own cell and changes nothing, `f(c)`; one taking `@c` may change it, `f(@c)`; a field is read in place, `c.n`
  fix (guess): read it in place, the caller's own cell and no copy: `b: Box lent`
  fix (guess): or, where the function changes it, take it by place and lend it at each call with `@`

